The training set shows that \(|d_{ij}|\) near 20 pm/V occurs for a small number of well-defined families: (i) tetragonal defect-chalcopyrite sulfides (CdGa\(_2\)S\(_4\) = 21.7, CuGaAgS\(_4\) = 21.2, AlHgS\(_4\) = 21.1), (ii) the orthorhombic Ca\(_8\)Cd\(_4\)P\(_8\) structure (20.3), and (iii) the layered Li–Mg–Ga–Se phases whose lattices sit at \(a\approx6.32\) Å, \(b\approx3.83\) Å (20.4).  

Direct lattice-and-composition matching of the 100 candidates to these three families immediately isolates five structures whose predicted tensors lie closest to the target:

- c097 (Li\(_2\)MgGa\(_2\)Se\(_5\)) reproduces the 6.32 Å / 3.90 Å metric of the 20.4 pm/V LiMgGaSe\(_3\) polytype;  
- c075 (AlGaCu\(_2\)S\(_4\)) is the Al/Cu analogue of the 21.2 pm/V chalcopyrite;  
- c087 (Ca\(_8\)Cd\(_4\)As\(_8\)) is the isostructural arsenide of the 20.3 pm/V phosphide (only a uniform 3 % volume expansion);  
- c093 (CuAlSe\(_2\)) is the Cu analogue of AlAgSe\(_2\) (15.6 pm/V) and therefore interpolates to \(\approx18\);  
- c051 (ZnGa\(_2\)S\(_4\)) is the Zn analogue of CdGa\(_2\)S\(_4\) (21.7 pm/V) and therefore interpolates to \(\approx16\)–18.

All other candidates belong to families whose training values are either \(\ll10\) (alkali halides, oxides) or \(\gg30\) (tellurides, phosphides, heavy-metal selenides) and are therefore farther from 20 pm/V.

Final: c097, c075, c087, c093, c051
